+# FAA archive association: exact accession, copy descriptions and remaining transfer gap
+
+October 30, 2026. B129 / PD04–PD05 original-record work-plan supplement. This is a dated acquisition/read result, not a replacement master list or a finding of preservation compliance, destruction or intent.
+
+## What changed
+
+**The actually inspected NARA series description explicitly links the FAA 9/11 collection to disposition authority N1-237-05-4 and accession NN3-237-09-007.** The disposition field matches the handwritten job label transcribed from the previously acquired schedule cover. This is stronger than a relationship inferred only from similar titles. It remains a **catalog-level association**, not the executed transfer document, item manifest or case-specific classification of a missing record. [Series 7419198](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/7419198), Control Numbers, pins P01–P02.
+
+The [preceding schedule study](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/8bc80894a40ac207b2ccce62a9fdd6d22d4c1139/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-911-special-schedule-2026-10-30/README.md) correctly recorded that the parent contents and an explicit association had not been acquired in that pass. Its bytes, uncertainties and failed access observations are unchanged. This later study adds an actual reading of the parent and copy details. It does not retroactively make the earlier access attempt successful or complete the remaining custody join.
+
+## What was actually acquired and read
+
+The public browser loaded series **7419198**, its expanded description and copy-details dialog, the first and last pages of its folder table, and the directly linked folder **7604277**. The latter was read at description/first-ten-item-title level only. No underlying item PDF, original transfer agreement, accession form or individual late-received record was downloaded or read in this pass. No authentication, hidden API, third-party contact or repeated broad search was used.
+
+| Preserved source representation | Captured UTC, October 30 | Bytes / SHA-256 |
+|---|---|---|
+| Expanded parent DOM and Copy 1 dialog | 13:43:26.121 | 18,344 / `54c41f10620a03de649b2f1326e0edd60e039602b39fa6eba97910c5e8531d5a` |
+| Parent folder table, page 11 of 11 | 13:44:16.321 | 14,803 / `6221e869d9a324ca70b06d2de02cb097cff2412dfea71f8c4fc468e2e750c72c` |
+| Late-received folder description and first table page | 13:44:55.750 | 13,629 / `6a02225237ff32085518e126dc6c7d1316b20449f7e99263fff03f814b67c717` |
+
+These hashes fingerprint **browser-rendered DOM snapshots**, not original server-response bytes, a native catalog export, a historical transfer, or the files counted on a storage device. Full snapshots remain local and are excluded from this public bundle. Source pins give exact heading/field and saved-snapshot line locators. Browser success establishes this observed representation was accessible; it does not explain the preceding web-reader failure.
+
+## Specific findings and competing limits
+
+### 1. A concrete accession target and matching authority label
+
+The parent Control Numbers section lists:
+
+- National Archives Identifier: **7419198**.
+- Accession Number: **NN3-237-09-007**.
+- Disposition Authority Number: **N1-237-05-4**.
+- HMS Record Entry ID: **HS1-70792448**.
+- HMS/MLR Entry Number: **UD-10D-1**.
+
+The alternate series title includes item **8020.5**, matching the schedule's item label. The direct authority-label match and identifiers materially narrow the next records target. They do not prove the accession's receipt date merely from its code, that every source original transferred, or that the 2006 correction/action files belonged to the accession. [Parent control fields](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/7419198), P01–P02; [original schedule](https://www.archives.gov/files/records-mgmt/rcs/schedules/departments/department-of-transportation/rg-0237/n1-237-05-004_sf115.pdf#page=1), H01.
+
+### 2. Preserve the differing quantities and their labels
+
+| Observed field | Value and scope | What has not been established |
+|---|---|---|
+| Parent table level | **104 File Units** | A census of every item or every original record. Only table pages 1 and 11 were inspected. |
+| Parent online availability | **14,165 Items**, with **14,166 digital objects**, currently ready to view | A count of distinct historical events, independent evidence, original transferred files, or specifically relevant correction records. |
+| Parent archived Copy 1 extent | **8,745 data files**; dialog also says **8745 Logical Data Record** | The counting rule, version/date, relationship to present online objects, or total originals that existed. |
+| Late-received folder | **3,077 Items** and **3,077 digital objects**, with partial-availability wording | Historical completeness, relevance of all entries, or identity of unlisted/unread contents. Only first ten titles were inspected. |
+
+Pins P03–P04 and P07. **No subtraction, missing-file total, percentage of disclosure, or percentage of proof is warranted from these fields.** Preserve the numbers as observed; the catalog uses different units/levels and supplies no acquired crosswalk between them. Their unequal values are a reconciliation target, not an established inventory deficit. A common item/object/file identifier manifest and count-definition/version history would permit an actual accounting test.
+
+### 3. Copy purposes and a general readability warning
+
+The parent labels archived Copy 1 **Reference, Reproduction, and Preservation**, on **Magnetic Disk: Hard Drive**. The expanded dialog describes those purposes and warns that some digital files may no longer be readable because media, readers, hardware or software are no longer easily available. [Parent archived-copy details](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/7419198), P04.
+
+The late-received folder's displayed copy lists **Reference and Reproduction**, also on a hard drive; the displayed purpose field does not also list Preservation. Preserve that difference without treating either level as controlling. A catalog purpose label is not a binary identity test, a certification that every original survives, or a finding that the child received no preservation. The warning is general: no file was demonstrated unreadable in this unit. Neither its cause nor affected item IDs are identified here. Pins P04/P08.
+
+### 4. A distinct late-received category, without an assumed deadline
+
+The parent arrangement describes seven subseries, ending in **Records Received After Deadline**. The last table page explicitly links [file unit 7604277](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/7604277) under that title. Its first ten listed item titles comprise a flight-strip entry and overtime/staff-overtime entries; underlying PDFs were not inspected. This does not describe all 3,077 entries and does not establish that any corrected QFR is included. The relevant deadline, receipt dates, source offices and selection rules remain unknown. Pins P05–P07.
+
+The parent dates distinguish **collected/maintained 2001–2004** from **coverage 1999–2004**. The description explicitly includes records about the 1999 Learjet N47BA accident as well as September 11 material. These dates and contents give important scope limits: not every item in the series is necessarily a substantive 9/11 operational record, much less evidence about the 2006 investigation. Conversely, series date metadata does not prove a particular later record is absent. We performed no comprehensive contents search or negative existence test. [Series dates, arrangement and description](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/7419198), P05.
+
+### 5. Availability, access and use are different source fields
+
+The parent says **Partially Available in the Catalog**, **Access: Partially Restricted**, and **Use: Possibly Restricted**, with FAA-redaction and possible-copyright notes. The child says **Partially Available**, **Access: Possibly Restricted**, and **Use: Unrestricted**. These observations remain side by side at their stated levels. Online availability is not the same as an exemption decision; a use field is not an access field. No current item-specific withholding or copyright determination is inferred. Pin P09. This bundle publishes original notes and safe selected fields, not source images, full DOM, staff contacts or record bodies.
+
+## Assessment and next discriminating records
+
+**High confidence in the observed catalog field association**, with preserved rendered snapshots and an exact string match to the previously transcribed job label. **Unknown**: actual transfer/acceptance, item-level custody/completeness, applicable copy classification, counting rules, identified readability losses, and inclusion of any missing correction/action record. Official catalog metadata is useful evidence for where to look; it is indirect evidence of the underlying historical transfer.
+
+The strongest objection to treating the count/copy differences as suspicious is that the fields describe different levels, purposes and units. That possibility is recorded, not adopted as a demonstrated explanation of the specific counts. An incomplete-preservation hypothesis likewise needs a defined original population, a matched manifest and actual disposition/retention evidence. No coordination, cover-up, improper disposal or motive follows from these fields alone.
+
+The next concrete target is the **transfer/accession dossier and attached item manifest for NN3-237-09-007**, joined through HS1-70792448 / UD-10D-1 / N1-237-05-4, including acceptance and any copy-generation/readability documentation. Missing FAA corrected answer/delivery (PD01), signed consideration/action/no-action (PD02), recommendation implementation/closure (PD03), and case-specific policy/classification (PD04) remain open. The original schedule-to-series question advances at catalog level only; no substantive gate is closed.
+
+[OPEN-RECORDS.md](OPEN-RECORDS.md) retains the specific TODOs and both-direction tests. All five tracks and eighteen substantive original-record acceptance criteria remain unfinished. Technical-owner recorder/materials/clock tests were not duplicated. [CHECKLIST.md](CHECKLIST.md), [SOURCE-PINS.json](SOURCE-PINS.json), [REVISION.diff](REVISION.diff) and [MANIFEST.json](MANIFEST.json) document scope, source locators, additive text changes and companion hashes. Actual commit/ref/file verification follows publication separately.
